            <div xml:id="d221">

                <pb facs="0477" n="361" sameAs="frus:frus1923v01/pg361"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">738.3915/244: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The High Commissioner in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">J. H. Russell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-07-14T14:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 14, 1923—2
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 6:40 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>100. Department’s 75, July 7, 5 p.m. President Borno has informed me that he
                    intends replying to my note accepting in principle <pb facs="0478" n="362"
                        xml:id="pg362"/> the question of negotiating at this time with the Dominican
                    Government with a view to the settlement of the boundary dispute by arbitration
                    but that he will request that negotiations be carried on at Port au Prince.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Russell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
